---
metadata:
  layer: root
  profile: root
  scope: ./
  version: "1.0"
  description: pi-norm-spec hybrid repository governance

template:
  required_files: [AGENTS.md, README.md, CHANGELOG.md, ROADMAP.md, Cargo.toml, package.json]
  required_directories: [crates/, docs/, extensions/, tests/]
  naming_convention:
    - "kebab-case for crate and planning directory names"
    - "kebab-case TypeScript extension filenames"
  single_source_of_truth:
    - source: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
      for: the Rust and TypeScript boundary
    - source: docs/decisions.md
      for: decisions and rationale
    - source: docs/planning/status.md
      for: current development state

agent_rules:
  update_order:
    - "Record protocol or enforcement decisions before implementation"
    - "Implement semantics in Rust and keep the TypeScript adapter thin"
    - "Run Rust, TypeScript, and applicable end-to-end gates"
  reference_policy:
    target_must_exist: true
    allow_external: false
    require_description: true

strong_references:
  - type: source
    target: /docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
    sync: auto_pull
    validation: strict
    description: Architecture defines which side owns each behavior
---

# Repository conventions

TypeScript adapts pi events; Rust owns the engine and bridge. Format semantics
remain upstream in norm-spec.
